  "question": {
    "text": "Consider the functions <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>:</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8477;</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8477;</mi></math> defined by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>12</mn></mfrac></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo></mtd><mtd><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8804;</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mtd><mtd><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>&#62;</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math><br />If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math> is the area of the region <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8477;</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8477;</mi><mo>:</mo><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8804;</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>min</mi><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math>, then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mi>&#945;</mi></math> is _____ ."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "6",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Plotting the diagram of the given function we have,</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0004_8120d089339f.png\" style=\"width: 396px; height: 300px;\" />Now by diagram we can see twice of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;will be the required area,</p><p>So, required area <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#183;</mo><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msubsup><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>12</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#183;</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><msubsup><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"\"><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow><mn>12</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mfenced><mn>0</mn><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#8901;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>&#8901;</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>12</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
